      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Psychogenic Secretions",
      "category": "defensive",
      "traits": [
        "aura",
        "mental"
      ],
      "text": "30 feet. A creature that enters the emanation must attempt a DC 36 Will save save.\n\nOn a failure, the creature is Stupefied 1 for 1 minute (Stupefied 2 and also Paralyzed for 1 round on a critical failure).\n\nA creature that succeeds at its save is temporarily immune to psychogenic secretions for 1 minute.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "aura",
          "slug": "psychogenic-secretions",
          "radius": 30,
          "traits": [
            "mental"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Consume Knowledge",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "mental",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "The thoughtmaw invades the mind of a creature within 100 feet and attempts to swallow its capacity for higher thought. The creature must attempt a DC 36 Will save save.\n\nUsing Consume Knowledge immediately ends any of the ability's previous effects on a different creature.\n\n---\n\nCritical Success The creature is unaffected.\n\nSuccess The creature is Slowed 1 for 1 round.\n\nFailure The creature is slowed 1 and can take no actions other than basic actions for 1 minute.\n\nCritical Failure As failure, and the thoughtmaw is Quickened for 1 minute. It can use this extra action to Stride, Strike, or Cast a Spell if the target had prepared spells or a spell repertoire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "spell",
      "name": "Inveigle",
      "rank": 2,
      "ref": "spells:spell/inveigle"
    }
  ],
  "text": "Xulgath thoughtmaws are inheritors of the xulgaths' ancient psychic legacy. They eagerly and liberally use their ability to extract knowledge from their foes to quicken their own prodigious intellects.",
